# --- Shell-redirection artifacts from the cmd.exe hook wiring -----------------
# Hooks run as `cmd /c ...` and the hook payload JSON is piped in on stdin;
# cmd consumes the leftover stdin and parses it as a command line, so any '>'
# inside that JSON (prompt text, memory content, commit-message text) acts as a
# redirection operator and drops a 0-byte file in the repo root named after the
# next token: "RAW->128" -> 128, "ECE 5.57% > 5%" -> 5%, "-> np.ndarray", etc.
# Harmless but noisy. Ignored so they can never be committed by accident.
# Real fix belongs in the hook config (give the hook a NUL stdin, or invoke node
# directly instead of through `cmd /c`); this is only a safety net.
# No legitimate root-level file in this repo starts with a digit or ends in '%'.
/[0-9]*
/*%
/IMG_SIZE
/np.ndarray
/proves